          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"jobId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"conversationId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"traceId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"supportingChunks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"nodes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"waitingToolCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"workflowCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"workflowVersion\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"workflowStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"startDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"createDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeTaken\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"inputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"outputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}",
          "type": "WORKFLOW"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHANGE_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Objective\n- Produce a concise summary title and a short explanatory subtitle, followed by one or more widgets that best match the user question and data.\n- Avoid duplicating the same data across text and widgets or across multiple widgets."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize Answer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767910711202"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ANSWER",
          "id": "1767819703835",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767819703838_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are an analyst answering manager questions about learning enrollments (“learner_records”). Use the provided data as the sole source of truth and produce a concise, management-ready answer focused on the people and/or items the user asks about. Questions may be learner-centric or learning-item–centric.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</user_question>\n- Learner-record data (authoritative):\n  <learner_records>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DATA_TO_ANSWER_QUERY.$output.output}}</learner_records>\n- Chat history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- Data history (optional; may include learner names/ids or item titles/ids):\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nGuidance\n- Data first: Base all statements strictly on learner_records; do not infer or fabricate missing details.\n- Context resolution (optional, secondary): Use data_history to resolve brief references (e.g., “that course,” “her,” “the first two”) only if those entities are also present in current learner_records. If still ambiguous, consult recent chat_history; otherwise ignore and answer based on what’s clearly in learner_records.\n- If history conflicts with current data, follow learner_records.\n- Scope: Records may represent learners→items or items→learners. Support both patterns.\n- For this Assigned Learning Monitor panel, interpret at-risk scope as overdue or due within 30 days, matching the panel definition.\n\nStatus interpretation (values only; for reasoning and wording)\n- completed: completion date present (or status meaning indicates completion).\n- overdue: due date in the past AND not completed.\n- due within 30 days: due date within the next 30 days (inclusive) AND not completed.\n- in progress / not started: use status meaning when available; if unclear, omit.\n\nAnswer style\n- Start with a direct answer in 1–2 sentences that addresses the user’s question.\n- Follow with compact, decision-focused details (counts, top items/people, notable dates) relevant to the question. Keep it concise.\n\nPrivacy\n- Reference only people/items present in learner_records.\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or internal IDs unless explicitly requested and present.\n- Preserve names exactly as they appear in the data.\n\nRobustness\n- Handle empty/malformed chat_history or data_history gracefully; never introduce entities not in learner_records.\n- If no relevant records match the request, output exactly: No relevant enrollments were found for this request."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
