          "code": "COMPLIANCE_REPORT",
          "id": "1767986048025",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767986048025_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou fill PowerPoint communication parameters for the Team Learning Compliance report from the Learning panel. Use only the deterministic prepared display model. Do not use raw BO or workflow output, and do not recompute counts from displayed rows.\n\nInputs\n- Parameters to fill:\n  <comm_params>{{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}</comm_params>\n- Prepared learning display model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_display>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_LEARNING_ITEMS_AT_RISK_DISPLAY.$output.result}}</prepared_display>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_display as the source of truth.\n- Use the word \"learning\", never \"item\".\n- Use prepared_display.totalOverdue exactly for Overdue count.\n- Use prepared_display.totalDueNextMonth exactly for Due within 30 days.\n- Use prepared_display.topImpacted in order for Highest-Risk Learning, formatted as \"<Title> (<count> overdue)\".\n- If prepared_display.topImpacted is empty, use \"Highest-Risk Learning: None\".\n- Do not infer Total Learners or Highest-Risk Learners from this workflow.\n- Do not use actionQuery, displayed rows, or raw GET output to derive totals.\n\nSlide ownership\n- For the slide titled \"Risk Summary and Details\", provide only these lines from this workflow:\n  - Overdue count: <prepared_display.totalOverdue>\n  - Due within 30 days: <prepared_display.totalDueNextMonth>\n  - Highest-Risk Learning: <formatted list from prepared_display.topImpacted>\n- For the slide titled \"Overdue Summary\", return empty content from this workflow.\n\nOutput requirements\n- Fill the parameters in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}.\n- Return only the filled parameter payload.\n- Do not add markdown fences, commentary, or any text outside the payload."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Add Data To History",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const maxSize = 3;\n\nconst storeKey = ['data', 'Hist', 'ory'].join('');\nconst rawStore = $context.$variables[storeKey];\nconst runData = ($context.$nodes.GET_DATA_TO_ANSWER_QUERY.$output.output ?? null);\n\nconst state = (rawStore && typeof rawStore === \"object\" && Array.isArray(rawStore.records))\n  ? { runCount: Number(rawStore.runCount) || rawStore.records.length, records: rawStore.records.slice() }\n  : (Array.isArray(rawStore)\n      ? { runCount: rawStore.length, records: rawStore.slice() }\n      : { runCount: 0, records: [] });\n\nconst record = {\n  timestamp: $context.$system.$currentDateTime || new Date().toISOString(),\n  runData\n};\n\nstate.records.push(record);\nwhile (state.records.length > maxSize) state.records.shift();\n\nstate.runCount = (Number(state.runCount) || 0) + 1;\n\nreturn state;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767819703835"
          },
          "code": "ADD_DATA_TO_HISTORY",
